# Scenario diag-stic2-vdelay-pass (plan 08-07, D-04, D-05, D-10): outcome pass, exit 0. The program ivs-diag-stic-2 through the
# project boot stub contract 2 with the zero graphics ROM and KEY_4 closed from tick 0: the first read of 01FE returns the low
# byte 7D, so the program writes scene 6 in every frame (one MOB, the vertical delay register at 0003 and the border extension
# register at 0003). The asserts are the hand-derived expectations of data/golden/diag-stic2-vdelay-pass.expect (derivation in
# docs/video/diag-stic-2-derivation.md, section (f), written before the program): the same lines in the same order as the
# committed block of that document, and the same as the .expect (golden-expect-drift). The hash and the probes are derived under
# the pinned defaults PD-8 and PD-9 (derivation, section (i)); the probes avoid the positions those pins move. It never halts.
ivss 1
id diag-stic2-vdelay-pass
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub-2
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-stic-2.ivsc
capture video 0 10
input at_tick=0 c0=KEY_4 c1=0x0
run-to 640000 ticks
assert halted == no
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 000A
assert mem 02F2 == 007D
assert mem 02F3 == 0006
assert frame 0 displayed == no
assert frame 5 displayed == yes
assert frame 5 hash == f2fd902318f8dcd49c236b24528c8d87dc3df4ce8f09ac9c9c29404cb3845094
assert frame 5 pixel 60 43 == 4
assert frame 5 pixel 80 51 == 2
assert frame 5 pixel 150 90 == 1
assert video count == 10
